Z||000008||Dan86gt3.8||10-02-2000||12:07 PM||||terry is that serries 1 or 2?  Did you ever get the axles figured out?  I am reall interested in that dogbone you have mounted just to the right of the dip stick.  I slung my cv boot again (thought we had cured that) but I really need to add a dogbone in and would love to see some close up pics or get the info on how you rigged yours up.  Did you paint the s/c and the valve covers?  If i didn't know anybetter I would think that was a 2.8....||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||10-02-2000||01:19 PM||||The engine is a 92 with a 94 70mm blower and TB and 92 pulley.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>The engine dogbone mount is from a 94 3800 U-van. It can be mounted on either side of the engine. <P>The red turned out to be (after reading the can), Ford Red and the black is Hammerite Black.<P>The axles are 94 Old Ciera axles (same as the U-van) with manual trans Fiero outer CV's swapped on. Auto CV's won't work. The axle is smaller. So far, the measurement is correct. The axles are in and so far so good.<P>The trans is the stock 4T60EHD (the only way to go on the SC engines).<P>The rear manifold was modified by removing the outlet to the cat and sealing it off. The crossover was then split to form a Fiero style Y pipe. The O2 was moved to that location. <P>The oil filter is remote with a cooler. <P>Other stuff, but ......||||reg||1
Z||000010||pollock||10-02-2000||02:07 PM||||"The trans is the stock 4T60EHD (the only way to go on the SC engines)."<P>Why is that? Strength? Electronics? Fit?<P>Looks like a super-clean install.  nice.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||10-02-2000||02:28 PM||||Mainly because the code in the ECM is written around it (lots of little details).<P>I've always found automatics to be better on blown engines. Optimized shift points, blah, blah, blah.....||||reg||1
